<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52017" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καί νύ </span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κε</span></b> ), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>and now</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. νύ κεν . . ἄσπετον ἤρατο κῦδος, εἰ
					μὴ . . </span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.373
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				8.90
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.50
			</span></i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. νύ κε δή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.530
				</span></i>
			: also folld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ</span> without
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.317
			</span></i>; by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλά</span>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				630
			</span></i>: with no protasis, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. νύ κεν ἐς δεκάτην γενεὴν ἕτερόν γ́
					ἔτι βόσκοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.325
				</span></i>
			.</div>
